# Copy to pydantic_backend/.env and fill in every value below `Settings` (config.py)
# validates when constructed — even for running a single-purpose script like gmail_auth.py,
# not just the full server — because `get_settings()` builds and validates the *entire*
# Settings model in one shot, regardless of which fields the calling code actually reads.
# So gmail_auth.py needs GMAIL_CLIENT_ID/SECRET, DATABASE_URL, LITELLM_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY,
# and LITELLM_WORKER_API_KEY all set too, even though it only ever touches the Gmail ones —
# there's no way to construct a partial Settings object. Reuse the exact same values already
# in your install/k8s/backend.env or install/docker/backend.env; these don't need to be
# different values, just present here too so pydantic-settings can validate the model.
#
# This file is gitignored (never commit it) via .env.* in .gitignore.

GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# URL-encode special characters in the password, e.g. @ -> %40
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:xyz@genai-gateway-postgresql.genai-gateway.svc.cluster.local:5432/tender_eval
LITELLM_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
LITELLM_WORKER_API_KEY=

# --- Everything below has a default in config.py — only set what you actually need locally ---
PARSER_BASE_URL=https://ei-api.mg2.eglb.intel.com/pdf-pipeline
LITELLM_BASE_URL=https://ei-api.mg2.eglb.intel.com/v1
LITELLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507
REVIEWER_EMAIL=navchetna.intel@gmail.com
